{{!-- One numbered entry in the pagination control.

	{{> "pagination-page" n=3}}             a link to page 3
	{{> "pagination-page" n=3 here=true}}   page 3, which is the page you are on

	n       the page number
	here    render it as the current page rather than as a link

Its own partial because pagination.hbs names five numbers — 1, `prev`, `page`, `next` and `pages`
— and each of them can be either state, so the two class lists would otherwise be written out
seven times between them. Nothing here needs the Tailwind scanner to see a duplicate: one literal
occurrence anywhere under the theme's `@source` glob compiles the class for the whole theme.

`{{page_url n}}` resolves against the request, so this works on the homepage collection and on the
Feed channel without either knowing its own URL. --}}
{{#if here}}
	<span
		aria-current="page"
		class="border-accent bg-accent text-on-accent font-ui rounded-sm border px-4 py-2.5 text-sm font-semibold">{{n}}</span>
{{else}}
	<a
		href="{{page_url n}}"
		class="border-border font-ui text-text hover:bg-surface-2 rounded-sm border px-4 py-2.5 text-sm no-underline">{{n}}</a>
{{/if}}
